* Lab 02-07 -- columns of resistance matrices R = G^-1, read off by injecting a unit current at one node.
* Column j of R is the vector of node voltages when 1 A (or 1 mA) is injected at node j and nothing else.
* Reciprocity check: R_kj measured by injecting at j equals R_jk measured by injecting at k.
*
* Example 02-07.2: 1-ohm ladder, ground-1-2-3-ground. Copy "a" injects 1 A at node 1, copy "b" at node 2.
* EXPECT va1 key:../../chapters/02-07-determinants-inverses-and-vector-spaces.md#Ex_02-07.2b rtol=1e-6
* EXPECT va2 key:../../chapters/02-07-determinants-inverses-and-vector-spaces.md#Ex_02-07.2h rtol=1e-6
* EXPECT va3 key:../../chapters/02-07-determinants-inverses-and-vector-spaces.md#Ex_02-07.2d rtol=1e-6
* EXPECT vb2 key:../../chapters/02-07-determinants-inverses-and-vector-spaces.md#Ex_02-07.2c rtol=1e-6
*
* Example 02-07.5: the circuit of Example 02-06.5. Copy "c" injects 1 mA at node 2, copy "d" at node 3 (volts = kOhm).
* EXPECT vc1 key:../../chapters/02-07-determinants-inverses-and-vector-spaces.md#Ex_02-07.5e rtol=1e-3
* EXPECT vc2 key:../../chapters/02-07-determinants-inverses-and-vector-spaces.md#Ex_02-07.5g rtol=1e-3
* EXPECT vc3 key:../../chapters/02-07-determinants-inverses-and-vector-spaces.md#Ex_02-07.5i rtol=1e-3
* EXPECT vd1 key:../../chapters/02-07-determinants-inverses-and-vector-spaces.md#Ex_02-07.5f rtol=1e-3
* EXPECT vd3 key:../../chapters/02-07-determinants-inverses-and-vector-spaces.md#Ex_02-07.5h rtol=1e-3
*
* Problem 02-07.11 (copy "e"), Problem 02-07.12 (copies "f", "g") and Problem 02-07.13 (copies "h", "k").
* EXPECT ve1 key:../../solutions/02-07-solutions.md#02-07.11b rtol=1e-3
* EXPECT ve2 key:../../solutions/02-07-solutions.md#02-07.11c rtol=1e-3
* EXPECT vf1 key:../../solutions/02-07-solutions.md#02-07.12b rtol=1e-6
* EXPECT vf2 key:../../solutions/02-07-solutions.md#02-07.12c rtol=1e-6
* EXPECT vg2 key:../../solutions/02-07-solutions.md#02-07.12d rtol=1e-6
* EXPECT vh1 key:../../solutions/02-07-solutions.md#02-07.13c rtol=1e-6
* EXPECT vh2 key:../../solutions/02-07-solutions.md#02-07.13d rtol=1e-6
* EXPECT vk1 key:../../solutions/02-07-solutions.md#02-07.13f rtol=1e-3
* EXPECT vk2 key:../../solutions/02-07-solutions.md#02-07.13g rtol=1e-3
* EXPECT vk3 key:../../solutions/02-07-solutions.md#02-07.13h rtol=1e-3
* EXPECT ik  key:../../solutions/02-07-solutions.md#02-07.13i scale=1e-3 rtol=1e-3

* ---- ladder, 1 A into node 1
Ia  0 a1 DC 1
Ra0 a1 0  1
Ra1 a1 a2 1
Ra2 a2 a3 1
Ra3 a3 0  1
* ---- ladder, 1 A into node 2
Ib  0 b2 DC 1
Rb0 b1 0  1
Rb1 b1 b2 1
Rb2 b2 b3 1
Rb3 b3 0  1

* ---- Example 02-06.5 circuit, 1 mA into node 2
Ic  0 c2 DC 1m
Rca c1 c2 1k
Rcb c1 c3 2k
Rcc c2 0  1k
Rcd c2 c3 2k
Rce c3 0  500
* ---- same circuit, 1 mA into node 3
Id  0 d3 DC 1m
Rda d1 d2 1k
Rdb d1 d3 2k
Rdc d2 0  1k
Rdd d2 d3 2k
Rde d3 0  500

* ---- Problem 02-06.11 / 02-07.11 circuit, 1 mA into node 1
Ie  0 e1 DC 1m
Re1 e1 0  2k
Re2 e1 e2 1k
Re3 e2 0  4k

* ---- Problem 02-07.12 pi network: 1 mA into port 1 (copy f), into port 2 (copy g)
If  0 f1 DC 1m
Rfs f1 f2 1k
Rf1 f1 0  500
Rf2 f2 0  1k
Ig  0 g2 DC 1m
Rgs g1 g2 1k
Rg1 g1 0  500
Rg2 g2 0  1k

* ---- Problem 02-07.13 bridge, balanced (h) and with the 3-0 resistor at 2k (k); 1 mA into node 1
Ih  0 h1 DC 1m
Rh12 h1 h2 1k
Rh13 h1 h3 1k
Rh23 h2 h3 1k
Rh20 h2 0  1k
Rh30 h3 0  1k
Ik  0 k1 DC 1m
Rk12 k1 k2 1k
Rk13 k1 k3 1k
Rk23 k2 k3 1k
Rk20 k2 0  1k
Rk30 k3 0  2k

.op
.control
op
let va1 = v(a1)
let va2 = v(a2)
let va3 = v(a3)
let vb2 = v(b2)
let vc1 = v(c1)
let vc2 = v(c2)
let vc3 = v(c3)
let vd1 = v(d1)
let vd3 = v(d3)
let ve1 = v(e1)
let ve2 = v(e2)
let vf1 = v(f1)
let vf2 = v(f2)
let vg2 = v(g2)
let vh1 = v(h1)
let vh2 = v(h2)
let vk1 = v(k1)
let vk2 = v(k2)
let vk3 = v(k3)
let ik = (v(k3) - v(k2))/1k
echo "va1 = $&va1"
echo "va2 = $&va2"
echo "va3 = $&va3"
echo "vb2 = $&vb2"
echo "vc1 = $&vc1"
echo "vc2 = $&vc2"
echo "vc3 = $&vc3"
echo "vd1 = $&vd1"
echo "vd3 = $&vd3"
echo "ve1 = $&ve1"
echo "ve2 = $&ve2"
echo "vf1 = $&vf1"
echo "vf2 = $&vf2"
echo "vg2 = $&vg2"
echo "vh1 = $&vh1"
echo "vh2 = $&vh2"
echo "vk1 = $&vk1"
echo "vk2 = $&vk2"
echo "vk3 = $&vk3"
echo "ik = $&ik"
.endc
.end
